01:16:25,423 --> 01:16:28,468
it tends to leave lots of low volume

1005
01:16:28,468 --> 01:16:32,655
areas as the market quickly moves away from prices being advertised.

1006
01:16:33,556 --> 01:16:36,356
There is a natural tendency for directional bias.

1007
01:16:36,356 --> 01:16:42,754
So over the period of the day, it'll feel as though a market constantly wants to go in one direction or another.

1008
01:16:44,356 --> 01:16:46,656
We have very short consolidation periods.

1009
01:16:46,756 --> 01:16:52,856
So again, we see initiative with a little bit of two-way trade. And that two-way trade doesn't last very long.

1010
01:16:53,456 --> 01:16:58,056
And the last one, we tend to break through a lot of key reference points.

1011
01:16:58,356 --> 01:17:04,593
If ever you felt as though a market wasn't respecting any kind of technicals or wasn't paying attention to any

1012
01:17:04,593 --> 01:17:11,453
kind of key pivots that you had noted, this is a very, very early characteristic that a market is trying to trend.

